  {
    "id": "mcp-search-tool",
    "toolName": "mcp__notion__search",
    "input": {
      "query": "Android density"
    },
    "expected": {
      "label": "mcp__notion__search",
      "detail": "Android density"
    },
    "android": false,
    "note": "Neither desktop nor mobile ever humanized an mcp__server__tool name - both showed it raw, so that is the shared rule. Native Android already humanizes it to \"Notion · Search\" (pre-existing, tested in ThreadPresentationTest.mcpNamespaceRemainsVisibleEvenWhenTheLeafMatchesABuiltInAlias); downgrading to the raw identifier would be a readability regression, so this is a documented, intentional divergence rather than a bug."
  },
